# Corpus pipeline (scan order)

When ranking mined candidates, authoring gate decisions, filing Smith
tickets, or running extract/fraction/batch on a new corpus, follow
[`docs/CORPUS-PIPELINE.md`](docs/CORPUS-PIPELINE.md). Setup/PAT/score-v1:
[`docs/MINE-SETUP.md`](docs/MINE-SETUP.md).

## Order

1. `rank-mine-candidates.py --limit N` (highest score first)
2. `probe-corpus-admission.py` → `author-gate-decision.py` (`--auto` only for
   restricted NO-GO; `--human` for go / triage-trial)
3. Commit `*_gate_decision.json` + ledger; **file Smith issues** (mine does
   not auto-file) — GO before triage-trial
4. Smith locally: materialize pin → **explicit `files:` allowlist** →
   `CORPUS_MANIFESTS` + `WAVE_CORPORA` → measure (≥0.30) → batch → PR
5. Ecma wave corpora: extractor `js_precise_dir` (not legacy `js_dir`)
6. Java: `java-html-sanitizer-triage.py --corpus NAME --pin --url [--files …]`
   (default stem `NAME_java`)

Mostly Python; `--llm-draft` never writes GO. Bugbot before merge on
non-trivial Smith PRs (see `pr-bugbot-before-merge`).
